IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`

-- scja3-s74-vexatious-litigants.l4: section 74 (vexatious litigants).
-- Layer 1, written from the text alone (SCJA1969.txt lines 4770-4832).
-- The appeal-permission function takes the court of s 29C as an input (seam 9 of PLAN.md) and passes NOTHING through.
-- The Singapore International Commercial Court is counted with the General Division through s 18C (fork S3-K1).

§ `Section 74: vexatious litigants`

-- src:4772 | 74.—(1) If, on an application made by the Attorney‑General, the
-- src:4773 | General Division is satisfied that any person has habitually and
-- src:4774 | persistently and without any reasonable ground instituted vexatious
-- src:4775 | legal proceedings in any court or subordinate court, whether against
-- src:4776 | the same person or against different persons, the General Division
-- src:4777 | may, after hearing that person or giving him or her an opportunity of
-- src:4778 | being heard, order that —
@ref s 74(1) ("the General Division") (src:4772-4778)
GIVEN court IS A Court
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74 the court is the General Division` MEANS
    CONSIDER court
    WHEN `General Division` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- counted with the General Division through s 18C (fork S3-K1)
    WHEN `Singapore International Commercial Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section names "the General Division" and no other court
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Helper: an answer that holds only where the court is the General Division.
GIVEN gate IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      answer IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74 the answer holds where the court is the General Division` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN answer
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:4772 | 74.—(1) If, on an application made by the Attorney‑General, the
-- src:4773 | General Division is satisfied that any person has habitually and
-- src:4774 | persistently and without any reasonable ground instituted vexatious
-- src:4775 | legal proceedings in any court or subordinate court, whether against
-- src:4776 | the same person or against different persons, the General Division
-- src:4777 | may, after hearing that person or giving him or her an opportunity of
-- src:4778 | being heard, order that —
-- src:4780 | (a) no legal proceedings may without the permission of the
-- src:4781 | General Division be instituted by that person in any court
-- src:4782 | or subordinate court; and
-- src:4786 | (b) any legal proceedings instituted by that person in any court
-- src:4787 | or subordinate court before the making of the order must
-- src:4788 | not be continued by him or her without such permission,
-- src:4789 | and such permission must not be given unless the General
-- src:4790 | Division is satisfied that the proceedings are not an abuse
-- src:4791 | of the process of the court and that there is prima facie
-- src:4792 | ground for the proceedings.
@ref s 74(1) (src:4772-4792)
-- "after hearing that person or giving him or her an opportunity of being heard" is a condition of the power.
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the Attorney-General applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the General Division is satisfied that the person has habitually and persistently and without any reasonable ground instituted vexatious legal proceedings in a court or subordinate court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the General Division has heard the person or given the person an opportunity of being heard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74(1) the General Division may order that the person institute and continue legal proceedings only with its permission` MEANS
    `s 74 the answer holds where the court is the General Division` (`s 74 the court is the General Division` court)
        (IF NOT (`the Attorney-General applies`
                 AND `the General Division is satisfied that the person has habitually and persistently and without any reasonable ground instituted vexatious legal proceedings in a court or subordinate court`)
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, on an application made by the Attorney-General, the General Division is satisfied that any person has habitually and persistently and without any reasonable ground instituted vexatious legal proceedings in any court or subordinate court"
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `the General Division has heard the person or given the person an opportunity of being heard`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, after hearing that person or giving him or her an opportunity of being heard"
              ELSE JUST FALSE)

-- src:4780 | (a) no legal proceedings may without the permission of the
-- src:4781 | General Division be instituted by that person in any court
-- src:4782 | or subordinate court; and
@ref s 74(1)(a) (src:4780-4782)
GIVEN `the General Division has made an order against the person under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has the permission of the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74(1)(a) the person may institute legal proceedings in a court or subordinate court` MEANS
    IF NOT `the General Division has made an order against the person under subsection (1)`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the restraint is that of "the order" under subsection (1), and the text says nothing of a person against whom there is none
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the person has the permission of the General Division`
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the restraint is "without the permission of the General Division", and the text grants nothing where there is permission
         THEN NOTHING
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no legal proceedings may without the permission of the General Division be instituted by that person in any court or subordinate court"
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4780 | (a) no legal proceedings may without the permission of the
-- src:4781 | General Division be instituted by that person in any court
-- src:4782 | or subordinate court; and
@ref s 74(1)(a) (the bar) (src:4780-4782)
GIVEN `the General Division has made an order against the person under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has the permission of the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74(1)(a) the bar on instituting legal proceedings in a court or subordinate court applies` MEANS
    IF NOT `the General Division has made an order against the person under subsection (1)`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the restraint is that of "the order" under subsection (1), and the text says nothing of a person against whom there is none
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the person has the permission of the General Division`
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the bar is "without the permission of the General Division", so with the permission it does not apply (fork S3-B6)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:4786 | (b) any legal proceedings instituted by that person in any court
-- src:4787 | or subordinate court before the making of the order must
-- src:4788 | not be continued by him or her without such permission,
-- src:4789 | and such permission must not be given unless the General
-- src:4790 | Division is satisfied that the proceedings are not an abuse
-- src:4791 | of the process of the court and that there is prima facie
-- src:4792 | ground for the proceedings.
@ref s 74(1)(b) (continuing proceedings) (src:4786-4792)
GIVEN `the General Division has made an order against the person under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the legal proceedings were instituted by the person before the order was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has the permission of the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74(1)(b) the person may continue the legal proceedings instituted before the order` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the General Division has made an order against the person under subsection (1)`
            AND `the legal proceedings were instituted by the person before the order was made`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the restraint is on "any legal proceedings instituted by that person ... before the making of the order"
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the person has the permission of the General Division`
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the restraint is "without such permission", and the text grants nothing where there is permission
         THEN NOTHING
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be continued by him or her without such permission"
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4786 | (b) any legal proceedings instituted by that person in any court
-- src:4787 | or subordinate court before the making of the order must
-- src:4788 | not be continued by him or her without such permission,
-- src:4789 | and such permission must not be given unless the General
-- src:4790 | Division is satisfied that the proceedings are not an abuse
-- src:4791 | of the process of the court and that there is prima facie
-- src:4792 | ground for the proceedings.
@ref s 74(1)(b) (continuing proceedings: the bar) (src:4786-4792)
GIVEN `the General Division has made an order against the person under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the legal proceedings were instituted by the person before the order was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has the permission of the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74(1)(b) the bar on continuing the legal proceedings instituted before the order applies` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the General Division has made an order against the person under subsection (1)`
            AND `the legal proceedings were instituted by the person before the order was made`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the restraint is on "any legal proceedings instituted by that person ... before the making of the order"
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the person has the permission of the General Division`
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the bar is "without such permission", so with the permission it does not apply (fork S3-B6)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:4786 | (b) any legal proceedings instituted by that person in any court
-- src:4787 | or subordinate court before the making of the order must
-- src:4788 | not be continued by him or her without such permission,
-- src:4789 | and such permission must not be given unless the General
-- src:4790 | Division is satisfied that the proceedings are not an abuse
-- src:4791 | of the process of the court and that there is prima facie
-- src:4792 | ground for the proceedings.
@ref s 74(1)(b) (giving permission) (src:4786-4792)
GIVEN `the General Division is satisfied that the proceedings are not an abuse of the process of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the General Division is satisfied that there is prima facie ground for the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74(1)(b) the General Division may give permission to continue the legal proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the General Division is satisfied that the proceedings are not an abuse of the process of the court`
       AND `the General Division is satisfied that there is prima facie ground for the proceedings`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): permission "must not be given unless" the General Division is satisfied of both; once it is, the text grants no permission of its own
    THEN NOTHING
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "such permission must not be given unless the General Division is satisfied that the proceedings are not an abuse of the process of the court and that there is prima facie ground for the proceedings"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4786 | (b) any legal proceedings instituted by that person in any court
-- src:4787 | or subordinate court before the making of the order must
-- src:4788 | not be continued by him or her without such permission,
-- src:4789 | and such permission must not be given unless the General
-- src:4790 | Division is satisfied that the proceedings are not an abuse
-- src:4791 | of the process of the court and that there is prima facie
-- src:4792 | ground for the proceedings.
@ref s 74(1)(b) (giving permission: the bar) (src:4786-4792)
GIVEN `the General Division is satisfied that the proceedings are not an abuse of the process of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the General Division is satisfied that there is prima facie ground for the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74(1)(b) the bar on giving permission to continue the legal proceedings applies` MEANS
    IF `the General Division is satisfied that the proceedings are not an abuse of the process of the court`
       AND `the General Division is satisfied that there is prima facie ground for the proceedings`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): permission "must not be given unless the General Division is satisfied that the proceedings are not an abuse of the process of the court and that there is prima facie ground for the proceedings", so once it is satisfied of both the bar does not apply (fork S3-B6)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:4798 | (2) If the person against whom an order is sought under
-- src:4799 | subsection (1) satisfies the General Division that he or she lacks
-- src:4806 | the means to retain an advocate and solicitor, the General Division is
-- src:4807 | to assign one to the person.
@ref s 74(2) (src:4798-4807)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `an order against the person is sought under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person satisfies the General Division that he or she lacks the means to retain an advocate and solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74(2) the General Division is to assign an advocate and solicitor to the person` MEANS
    `s 74 the answer holds where the court is the General Division` (`s 74 the court is the General Division` court)
        (IF `an order against the person is sought under subsection (1)`
            AND `the person satisfies the General Division that he or she lacks the means to retain an advocate and solicitor`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the person against whom an order is sought under subsection (1) satisfies the General Division that he or she lacks the means to retain an advocate and solicitor, the General Division is to assign one"
         ELSE JUST FALSE)

-- src:4811 | (2A) A person against whom the General Division makes an order
-- src:4812 | under subsection (1) may bring an appeal against the order only with
-- src:4813 | the permission of the court to which the appeal is to be made under
-- src:4814 | section 29C.
@ref s 74(2A) (src:4811-4814)
-- Seam 9 of PLAN.md is an input: `s 29C the court to which the appeal is to be made`.
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the order is an order made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 29C the court to which the appeal is to be made` IS A MAYBE Court
GIVETH A MAYBE Court
`s 74(2A) the court whose permission is needed to appeal against the order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 74 the court is the General Division` court
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the order is an order made under subsection (1)`
        THEN `s 29C the court to which the appeal is to be made`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is about "an order under subsection (1)"
        ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is about an order of the General Division
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:4811 | (2A) A person against whom the General Division makes an order
-- src:4812 | under subsection (1) may bring an appeal against the order only with
-- src:4813 | the permission of the court to which the appeal is to be made under
-- src:4814 | section 29C.
@ref s 74(2A) ("only with the permission") (src:4811-4814)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the order is an order made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74(2A) the person may appeal against the order without permission` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 74 the court is the General Division` court
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the order is an order made under subsection (1)`
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may bring an appeal against the order only with the permission of the court to which the appeal is to be made under section 29C"
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is about "an order under subsection (1)"
        ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is about an order of the General Division
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:4820 | (3) No appeal lies from an order refusing permission under
-- src:4821 | subsection (1) for institution or continuance of legal proceedings.
@ref s 74(3) (src:4820-4821)
GIVEN `the order refuses permission under subsection (1) for the institution or continuance of legal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74(3) an appeal lies from the order refusing permission` MEANS
    IF `the order refuses permission under subsection (1) for the institution or continuance of legal proceedings`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No appeal lies from an order refusing permission under subsection (1) for institution or continuance of legal proceedings."
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is about "an order refusing permission under subsection (1)"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4827 | (4) A copy of any order under subsection (1) must be published in
-- src:4828 | the Gazette.
@ref s 74(4) (src:4827-4828)
GIVEN `an order has been made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74(4) a copy of the order must be published in the Gazette` MEANS
    IF `an order has been made under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is about "any order under subsection (1)"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4830 | (5) In this section, “legal proceedings” includes any proceedings,
-- src:4831 | process, action, application or appeal in any civil matter,
-- src:4832 | quasi‑criminal matter or criminal matter.
@ref s 74(5) (src:4830-4832)
DECLARE `s 74(5) kind of thing` IS ONE OF
    `s 74(5) proceedings`
    `s 74(5) process`
    `s 74(5) action`
    `s 74(5) application`
    `s 74(5) appeal`
    `s 74(5) another kind of thing`

GIVEN kind IS A `s 74(5) kind of thing`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74(5) the thing is within legal proceedings for section 74` MEANS
    -- all three kinds of matter are named in the subsection (a civil matter, a quasi-criminal matter and a criminal matter), so the kind of matter does not change the answer
    IF NOT (kind EQUALS `s 74(5) another kind of thing`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "legal proceedings" "includes" the things listed in a civil, quasi-criminal or criminal matter, and the text does not close the list
    ELSE NOTHING
